## 1. Executive Summary

The project aims to deliver an Azure‑based serverless web application that provides AI‑driven role‑play training for sales associates. The solution will enable on‑demand practice during lull periods, capture performance scores, and deliver reporting to drive attach‑rate improvements. Key decisions include using Azure OpenAI for the conversational engine, Azure AD B2C for secure multi‑tenant authentication, and a lean MVP architecture that avoids over‑engineering while retaining IP ownership for future partner roll‑outs. The recommendation is to proceed with the proposed MVP, leveraging the outlined Azure services to meet the budget, timeline, and scalability requirements.

---

## 2. Background Summary

The client currently relies on a single trainer to support 135 stores, resulting in limited training capacity, inconsistent role‑play experiences, and insufficient feedback for managers. Existing processes lack real‑time practice opportunities and detailed performance analytics, leading to missed upsell potential during sales floor lull periods.

